From: Rob Vogelaar <rob.vogelaar@libertyglobal.com>
Date: Mon, 31 Aug 2026 09:20:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] wifi_em: clean partial AP metrics reports on bad radio IDs

ap_report_push_cb() may already hold per-VAP link- and traffic-metric
allocations when a later configured radio ID is invalid. Returning directly
leaks that partial report. Send the failure through the common cleanup
boundary instead.

The fresh upstream OneWifi source already walks all fixed per-radio VAP slots
and releases its encoded output (RDKBWIFI-498), so the earlier version of this
backport no longer needs to duplicate that cleanup-loop change.

This is a generic OneWifi ownership correction, not an hwsim workaround.

Upstream-Status: Pending
---
diff --git a/source/apps/em/wifi_em.c b/source/apps/em/wifi_em.c
index bc355e9..8741333 100644
--- a/source/apps/em/wifi_em.c
+++ b/source/apps/em/wifi_em.c
@@ -1954,8 +1954,8 @@ static int ap_report_push_cb(em_ap_report_callback_arg_t *args)
         if (radio == NULL) {
             wifi_util_error_print(WIFI_EM, "%s:%d: NULL Pointer of radio_index %d\n", __func__,
                 __LINE__, radio_index);
-            free(data);
-            return RETURN_ERR;
+            rc = RETURN_ERR;
+            goto cleanup;
         }
         vap_map = &radio->vaps.vap_map;
 

